    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Structural pattern</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Tier 2</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Media.net</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Amazon</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Proxy</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">A stand-in that looks exactly like the real object but decides when, whether and how the real object is reached. Build virtual, protection, remote, caching and rate-limiting proxies, see how Java dynamic proxies power Spring, and learn to separate Proxy from Decorator and Adapter in one sentence each.</p>\n"
